@startuml
title P3 End-to-end Encrypted Media Components
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Sender Pulsar" {
  component "Local Media Prep\nnormalize / encode / encrypt" as SenderPrep
  component "E2EE Key Store\ncurrent epochs / grants" as SenderKeys
  component "Grant + Report Consent UI" as SenderConsent
}

package "Coordinator" {
  component "Ciphertext Router\nupload / fetch / schedule" as Router
  component "Epoch + Grant Service\njoin / leave / revoke" as Epochs
  component "Report Service\nmetadata + evidence audit" as Reports
  database "Opaque Object Storage\nciphertext + manifests" as Objects
  database "Identity + Air + Target Snapshot Store" as IdentityStore
}

package "Recipient Pulsar" {
  component "Grant + Recovery UI" as RecipientGrant
  component "E2EE Key Store\ncurrent epochs / grants" as RecipientKeys
  component "Decrypt Cache + Playback" as RecipientPlay
  component "Voluntary Evidence Export" as RecipientExport
}

package "Moderation" {
  component "Operator Review Surface\nexplicit evidence only" as Moderator
}

SenderPrep --> SenderKeys : media keys / recipient wraps
SenderPrep --> Router : ciphertext + manifest\n(no plaintext media)
SenderConsent --> SenderPrep : explicit send / grant intent

Router --> Objects : store opaque blobs
Router --> Epochs : resolve epoch + recipients
Epochs --> IdentityStore : Air members / roles /\ntarget snapshots / revokes
Reports --> IdentityStore : actor / policy checks
Reports --> Objects : evidence package refs

Router --> RecipientPlay : manifest + ciphertext refs
Epochs --> RecipientGrant : grant / transfer / recovery state
RecipientGrant --> RecipientKeys : accepted epochs / grants
RecipientPlay --> RecipientKeys : unwrap keys / verify epochs
RecipientExport --> Reports : optional decrypted evidence copy

Moderator --> Reports : read audit + provided evidence

note right of Router
Coordinator routes ciphertext, manifests,
wrapped keys, and audit metadata only.
It must not decode protected media.
end note

note right of RecipientExport
Decrypted evidence exists only when a
recipient explicitly exports it for a report.
No hidden server decrypt path is allowed.
end note

note bottom of SenderKeys
Key material remains in OS secure storage
on Pulsar clients, not in coordinator rows.
end note
@enduml
